# Wttrman Release Notes

## 1.0.0 (12 Feb 2025)

### New Features

- Initial release

## 1.2.2 (14 Mar 2025)

### Improvements

- Updated file structure to UV instead of BeeWare

### Bug Fixes

- Removed unneeded functions and generalized the remaining one

## 1.2.3 (31 Oct 2025)

### Improvements

- Bumped version to bring required Python version down to 3.10

## 1.2.4 (23 Jun 2026)

### Improvements

- Version bump for dependency updates

## 1.2.6 (21 Jul 2026)

### Improvements

- Version bump for dependency updates

## 1.2.27 (26 Oct 2026)

### Improvements

- Version bump for dependency updates
- Version bump for Python version bump to 3.15

## 2.0.0 (13 Nov 2026)

### New Features

- Added support for international locations (Canada, Australia, New Zealand, Japan, Germany, France, Ireland, United Kingdom, and United States)
- Added a full Preferences dialog to manage application settings
- Added customizable weather output metrics (Condition, Temperature, Feels Like, Wind, Humidity, Precipitation, Pressure, and UV Index)
- Added a toggleable Emoji icon system to replace the default plain-text weather conditions
- Added the ability to choose between Metric and USCS units
- Added configurable "Startup Defaults" for country, region, and city
- Added a dynamic grid-based weather output layout that wraps and scales based on window size
- Added an About dialog (Help → About Wttrman) showing version, author, and license

### Improvements

- Completely overhauled the UI to a modern, card-based layout with dynamic font scaling
- Refactored the codebase into modular components (`LocationPanel`, `WeatherPanel`, `PreferencesDialog`, `AboutDialog`, `LocationRepository`, `ThemeManager`)
- Replaced the monolithic `locations.yaml` with scalable, per-country JSON location files
- Replaced the legacy inline styling with a fully dynamic QSS theme system
- Added 12 built-in themes (Wttrman Dark/Light, Phaino Dark/Light, Catppuccin, Gruvbox, Solarized, Equinox)
- Implemented live theme switching in the Preferences dialog
- Improved the custom dropdown behavior to prevent full-screen lists and properly display scrollbars
- Added "session restore" logic to remember the last opened location on startup

### Bug Fixes

- Fixed the application crashing when querying invalid UV Index data from wttr.in
- Fixed an issue where the "Feels Like" checkbox did not visually gray out when disabled
- Fixed an issue where the "Feels Like" state was not remembered after toggling Temperature off and on
- Fixed text wrapping in the weather output so that emojis stay bound to their respective values (e.g., preventing "km/h" from breaking across lines)
- Fixed dropdown menus appearing blocky, misaligned, or having invisible scrollbars
